  "placementWarnings": [
    "boat-ktourmap.html pin [126.7074824191,35.0027033036] lies across the river near the sports park. Do not use it for the official south-bank lighthouse landing reconstruction.",
    "The exact position and direction of a moored boat changes. Model the photographed mooring arrangement as an estimated scene placement.",
    "Current official photos show a tiled-cabin Najuho and a larger brown vessel with two flat-roof cabins and blue/red flags. They do not show large yellow working sails raised.",
    "Historical sail imagery can inform a separate illustrative vessel or mural, but must not be described as the exact present-day moored fleet.",
    "Use the OSM bank for geographic arrangement, and official photos for deck height and retaining wall form; no exact surveyed elevation is available."
  ],
  "photoObservations": {
    "landing": [
      "The riverside road is elevated above a broad lower dark-brown timber deck, reached by a very wide stair with silver anti-slip strips and yellow landing strips.",
      "The lighthouse stands against a near-vertical concrete retaining wall at the lower deck. Upper deck railings are silver metal horizontal rails; outer edges of stairs have brown railings.",
      "The retaining wall has blue/turquoise and ochre maritime murals, with rhythmically spaced triangular buttresses. Make original stylised motifs instead of embedding copyrighted mural photography.",
      "A narrow white/light-grey triangulated metal gangway runs down from the landing toward a floating charcoal rectangular ticket/waiting structure beside the tiled-cabin boat.",
      "Lower deck edge contains black rubber fenders, cleats and mooring ropes; broad stair structures with triangular wooden side-cheeks bridge into the large tourist boat."
    ],
    "lighthouse": [
      "White cylindrical concrete shaft supports a widening flared cone with radial supports, circular balcony and white slender metal railing.",
      "Upper lantern room is short cylindrical white housing with small rectangular windows and shallow projecting circular cap; this is not a tall conical red-roof lighthouse.",
      "Black-and-white water-gauge scale is on the shaft; low timber fence and a slim freestanding grey interpretation slab surround the bottom."
    ],
    "najuho": [
      "Deep brown plank hull with slightly raised ends, open fore/aft seating, timber perimeter railing with two horizontal bars, side decks around a glazed central wooden cabin.",
      "Cabin roof is grey tiled Korean hipped-gable form, sharply upturned eaves with cyan/blue ornamental end pieces.",
      "Rectangular framed windows with green/blue reflected glazing; brown doors. Orange ring buoys on cabin sides.",
      "Yellow fender ropes/bundles hang down from the hull in four or more locations. Red flag with yellow emblem and blue flag with yellow dragon appear at opposite ends.",
      "Scale estimate from photo only: approximately 18-22 m long and 5-6 m broad; do not treat as a measured specification."
    ],
    "largeBoat": [
      "Long deep brown hull with upturned ends, two separated low rectangular flat-roof timber cabins, turquoise/green windows, open deck and long perimeter seating.",
      "Four tall silver-grey flag poles carry blue, white and red flags. There are orange/cream ring buoys, ropes and box-like wood deck fixtures.",
      "Scale estimate from photo only: approximately 27-32 m long and 7-9 m broad; do not treat as a measured specification."
    ],
    "street": [
      "The walk from the dock to the gallery passes the south end of Yeongsangyo. Cross from Deungdae-gil to the northeast-running Yeongsan 3-gil lane.",
      "The riverfront is Seonchang-gil north of the shops; Yeongsan 3-gil runs through the narrow shop cluster approximately parallel, then bends northeast to the gallery.",
      "Hong-eo storefronts are mostly low 1-2 storey masonry/plaster volumes, often blue or green roofs, red/blue/white large Korean signs and awnings; do not invent exact store identities where facade references are missing."
    ]
  },
